From 8263c3841ca595045c09b4c530442170b8374a5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:09:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci-review): leave room after the capped re-refresh delay
 and mark budget-skipped targeted PRs failed [daveey]

PR #1907 review 5887164857 follow-ups:
- MAX_REFRESH_DELAY_S 600 -> 480: a manual dispatch asking for >= 600 s spent the
  whole run budget before its first download attempt, so the PR was skipped with
  no mark and 'running on' stood. The headroom test now requires two full attempts
  and the first retry wait after the capped wait, not mere equality.
- A targeted run whose budget gate skips a PR now marks it 'refresh failed on <head>'
  (the sweep still writes nothing).
- Document the same-head 'Re-run failed jobs' gap in mark_refresh_failed.
- test_attempt_cost_matches_the_download_timeouts patches the openers and asserts
  the timeout= values instead of reading source (AGENTS.md).
---
 .github/workflows/ci-review-comment.yml |  2 +-
 scripts/ci/batch_review_comments.py     | 43 +++++++++---
 tests/ci/test_batch_review_comments.py  | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

